In article <dtoler.911021183921@tesla.ee.eng.auburn.edu> dtoler@eng.auburn.edu (Darren W. Toler) writes:
>I have a few questions that aren't quite covered in the spoilers file...
>(I'll try not to say anything that might be a spoilers in the questions though)

They're not?

>Is it possible to get a djinni from a glowing potion? If so, how?

Look in the WISHING section.  As for how - quaff the potion!

>Does a cursed wand of polymorph always have the same effect when you engrave 
>with it? 

Try looking at the very beginning of WAND EFFECTS.

>Do genecide scrolls work on monsters throughout the game or just on the level
>you are on?

Last time I checked, genocide meant killing *all* (yes, absolutely every
one) of a given creature, such that it can never exist again.

>Which artifacts can you #name? Do you have to be a certain alignment to do 
>that?

Look in the ARTIFACTS section.  No, you don't have to be a given alignment.

>Do pets gain intrinsics from dead monster corpses? My pet kept polymorphing 
>every few turns in one game so I assume it was from something he ate.

No, pets don't.  Probably your pet was hitting a polymorph trap, or perhaps
had been polymorphed into a chameleon.

>Does holy water hurt a vampire? (I watched Fright Night last night... :-)

Try looking under POTION THROWING EFFECTS.

Please forgive if I sound condescending.  A brief hint for those of you
using the spoilers:  Use the search function on your file viewer or editor
when checking the spoilers.  Searching for "water," for instance, would
turn up all references to holy water, including the information in 
POTION THROWING EFFECTS which tells that holy water _can_ damage undead
creatures.

